Reading the script line by line became just as important as understanding the vulnerability itself.
At the same time, I was also learning to use Visual Studio Code, which added another layer of learning.
Something that might take an experienced developer only a few minutes required considerably more time because I was developing two skills simultaneously:

* Understanding Python automation.
* Becoming comfortable with the development environment used to execute it.
Looking back, I do not consider that time wasted.

Understanding automation is an important step toward becoming a better security professional.
