# Security Impact

Weak brute-force protection allows attackers to repeatedly test passwords until valid credentials are discovered.

Even when an application appears to defend against repeated login attempts, implementation mistakes can completely undermine those protections.
Because authentication protects access to user accounts, weaknesses in brute-force defenses can lead to unauthorized access and account compromise.

---

-Defensive Recommendations
Implement robust server-side rate limiting.
Avoid relying on client-controlled information when identifying request sources.
Combine rate limiting with account lockout policies where appropriate.Monitor authentication attempts for abnormal behavior.
* Continuously test defensive mechanisms to ensure they cannot be bypassed through logic flaws.

